{"type":"message","id":"a4728832","parentId":"ff280d3e","timestamp":"2026-02-11T15:01:27.864Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It seems that I am unable to install Internet Explorer due to system command restrictions and lack of administrator privileges. Internet Explorer is primarily designed for Windows systems, and its installation on Linux may not be straightforward or even feasible.\n\nHere are some potential alternatives to consider:\n\n1. **Use Wine**: A compatibility layer to run Windows applications on Linux.\n2. **Virtual Machine**: Set up a Windows VM using software like VirtualBox or VMware.\n3. **Remote Access**: Access a Windows machine with Internet Explorer installed remotely.\n\nIf you need information on how to proceed with any of these options, let me know!","textSignature":"msg_058b208b594e3f4901698c99c5a7d08197b5e36aab4a6626af"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-4o-mini","usage":{"input":157,"output":125,"cacheRead":6144,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":6426,"cost":{"input":0.00002355,"output":0.000075,"cacheRead":0.0004915200000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00059007}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1770822085155}}
